45c8a9be-2c87-459e-a80a-ef2a68fbc884	5a959e92-2376-40c8-b3b2-e6f29c23b2af	assistant	To find the player who did the most number of tours, we need to query the `rankings` table to find the maximum number of tours and then join this result with the `players` table to get the first name and country code of that player.\n\n```sql\nSELECT p.first_name, p.country_code\nFROM players p\nJOIN (\n  SELECT player_id, MAX(tours) as max_tours\n  FROM rankings\n  GROUP BY player_id\n) r ON p.player_id = r.player_id\nWHERE r.max_tours = (\n  SELECT MAX(tours)\n  FROM rankings\n);\n```\n\nHowever, if there are multiple players with the same maximum number of tours, the above query will return all of them.\n\nAlternatively, you can use a window function to achieve the same result:\n\n```sql\nSELECT first_name, country_code\nFROM (\n  SELECT p.first_name, p.country_code,\n         RANK() OVER (ORDER BY r.tours DESC) as rank\n  FROM players p\n  JOIN rankings r ON p.player_id = r.player_id\n) t\nWHERE rank = 1;\n```\n\nThis query will also return all players with the maximum number of tours. \n\nBut if you are sure that there is only one player who did the most number of tours, you can use:\n\n```sql\nSELECT p.first_name, p.country_code\nFROM players p\nJOIN rankings r ON p.player_id = r.player_id\nORDER BY r.tours DESC\nLIMIT 1;\n```	SELECT p.first_name, p.country_code\nFROM players p\nJOIN (\n  SELECT player_id, MAX(tours) as max_tours\n  FROM rankings\n  GROUP BY player_id\n) r ON p.player_id = r.player_id\nWHERE r.max_tours = (\n  SELECT MAX(tours)\n  FROM rankings\n);	2026-04-30 21:52:37.819055+07	chat	null
