ce773ded-878f-4d2f-9b9b-1e0742597d41	8a3367db-b210-4902-9acc-5ddaff014a55	assistant	To find the number of visitors who did not visit any museum opened after 2010, we need to first identify the museums that were opened after 2010. Then, we find the visitors who visited these museums. Finally, we count the total number of visitors and subtract the number of visitors who visited these museums.\n\n```sql\nWITH museums_opened_after_2010 AS (\n  SELECT Museum_ID\n  FROM museum\n  WHERE Open_Year > '2010'\n),\nvisitors_of_these_museums AS (\n  SELECT DISTINCT visitor_ID\n  FROM visit\n  WHERE Museum_ID IN (SELECT Museum_ID FROM museums_opened_after_2010)\n)\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS num_visitors\nFROM visitor\nWHERE ID NOT IN (SELECT visitor_ID FROM visitors_of_these_museums);\n```\n\nThis query works as follows:\n\n1. The first Common Table Expression (CTE), `museums_opened_after_2010`, selects the IDs of museums that were opened after 2010.\n\n2. The second CTE, `visitors_of_these_museums`, selects the IDs of visitors who visited these museums.\n\n3. The main query then selects the IDs of visitors who are not in the list of visitors who visited these museums and counts them.\n\nNote that this query assumes that a visitor may visit a museum multiple times, but this is not reflected in the sample data provided. \n\nAlso note that if a visitor's ID is `NULL`, this query will not count them. If you want to count visitors with `NULL` IDs as well, you should use a `LEFT JOIN` instead. \n\nHowever, given the provided schema, visitor IDs seem to be `INT` and `NOT NULL`, so this should not be an issue here. \n\nThe query can be optimized by combining the two CTEs into one:\n\n```sql\nWITH visitors_of_museums_opened_after_2010 AS (\n  SELECT DISTINCT v.visitor_ID\n  FROM visit v\n  JOIN museum m ON v.Museum_ID = m.Museum_ID\n  WHERE m.Open_Year > '2010'\n)\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS num_visitors\nFROM visitor\nWHERE ID NOT IN (SELECT visitor_ID FROM visitors_of_museums_opened_after_2010);\n```	WITH museums_opened_after_2010 AS (\n  SELECT Museum_ID\n  FROM museum\n  WHERE Open_Year > '2010'\n),\nvisitors_of_these_museums AS (\n  SELECT DISTINCT visitor_ID\n  FROM visit\n  WHERE Museum_ID IN (SELECT Museum_ID FROM museums_opened_after_2010)\n)\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS num_visitors\nFROM visitor\nWHERE ID NOT IN (SELECT visitor_ID FROM visitors_of_these_museums);	2026-05-01 10:29:17.852116+07	chat	null
