613b639e-ac36-40f4-9dc6-5a9b9ccbd7d1	2a43158d-f78b-4fd6-8f45-6a3d86ee8c88	assistant	# Step-by-step analysis of the problem:\n1. **Understanding the error**: The error message indicates that the column `o.order_date` does not exist in the `orders` table. \n2. **Checking the schema**: Upon reviewing the provided schema for the `orders` table, it appears that there is no column named `order_date`. However, there is a column named `created_date` of type `TIMESTAMP`, which could potentially be used for date-related queries.\n\n# Fixed solution:\n```sql\nWITH\n  -- Tổng số đơn hàng, đơn hàng giao thành công, doanh thu và số đơn huỷ của mỗi cửa hàng\n  store_performance AS (\n    SELECT\n      s.id AS store_id,\n      s.store_name AS store_name, \n      COUNT(o.id) AS total_orders,\n      SUM(\n        CASE\n          WHEN o.order_status = 'Đã giao' THEN 1\n          ELSE 0\n        END\n      ) AS completed_orders,\n      SUM(\n        CASE\n          WHEN o.order_status = 'Đã giao' THEN o.total_after_discount\n          ELSE 0\n        END\n      ) AS total_revenue,\n      SUM(\n        CASE\n          WHEN o.order_status = 'Đã huỷ' THEN 1\n          ELSE 0\n        END\n      ) AS canceled_orders\n    FROM\n      orders o\n      JOIN stores s ON o.store_id = s.id\n    WHERE\n      o.created_date >= '2025-10-01'\n      AND o.created_date <= '2025-12-31'\n    GROUP BY\n      s.id,\n      s.store_name\n  ),\n  -- Tỷ lệ huỷ đơn của mỗi cửa hàng\n  store_cancel_rate AS (\n    SELECT\n      store_id,\n      store_name,\n      total_orders,\n      completed_orders,\n      total_revenue,\n      canceled_orders,\n      ROUND((canceled_orders * 1.0 / total_orders) * 100, 2) AS cancel_rate\n    FROM\n      store_performance\n  ),\n  -- Món ăn bán chạy nhất của mỗi cửa hàng\n  best_selling_food AS (\n    SELECT\n      od.store_id,\n      od.food_id,\n      SUM(od.quantity) AS total_quantity\n    FROM\n      order_detail od\n      JOIN orders o ON od.order_id = o.id\n    WHERE\n      o.created_date >= '2025-10-01'\n      AND o.created_date <= '2025-12-31'\n      AND o.order_status = 'Đã giao'\n    GROUP BY\n      od.store_id,\n      od.food_id\n  ),\n  -- Lấy ID món ăn bán chạy nhất của mỗi cửa hàng\n  best_selling_food_id AS (\n    SELECT\n      store_id,\n      food_id AS best_selling_food_id,\n      ROW_NUMBER() OVER (\n        PARTITION BY\n          store_id\n        ORDER BY\n          total_quantity DESC\n      ) AS rn\n    FROM\n      best_selling_food\n  )\n  -- Kết hợp các thông tin\nSELECT\n  scr.store_id,\n  scr.store_name,\n  scr.total_orders,\n  scr.completed_orders,\n  scr.total_revenue,\n  scr.cancel_rate,\n  bsf.best_selling_food_id\nFROM\n  store_cancel_rate scr\n  JOIN best_selling_food_id bsf ON scr.store_id = bsf.store_id\n  AND bsf.rn = 1\nORDER BY\n  scr.store_id;\n```\n\n# Explanation of changes:\n* **Replaced `o.order_date` with `o.created_date`**: Since the `orders` table does not have an `order_date` column, I replaced all instances of `o.order_date` with `o.created_date`, assuming that `created_date` is the intended column for date filtering.\n\n# Tests and example uses:\nYou can test this query by running it on your database and verifying that it produces the expected results. Make sure to check for any stores that have no orders within the specified date range to ensure that the query handles such cases correctly.	WITH\n  -- Tổng số đơn hàng, đơn hàng giao thành công, doanh thu và số đơn huỷ của mỗi cửa hàng\n  store_performance AS (\n    SELECT\n      s.id AS store_id,\n      s.store_name AS store_name, \n      COUNT(o.id) AS total_orders,\n      SUM(\n        CASE\n          WHEN o.order_status = 'Đã giao' THEN 1\n          ELSE 0\n        END\n      ) AS completed_orders,\n      SUM(\n        CASE\n          WHEN o.order_status = 'Đã giao' THEN o.total_after_discount\n          ELSE 0\n        END\n      ) AS total_revenue,\n      SUM(\n        CASE\n          WHEN o.order_status = 'Đã huỷ' THEN 1\n          EL