21159e93-9af6-4564-867a-c0bebdd34167	2f8f53f0-6e17-4a5e-ad2b-c67e9384a564	assistant	### Query Description\n\nThe following SQL query retrieves a list of stores that have had at least one order with a promotion applied. For each store, it provides the total revenue for Q4 2025, the number of canceled orders, the best-selling food item in history, and the average rating of the store.\n\n### SQL Query\n\n```sql\nWITH \n  -- Revenue for Q4 2025\n  store_revenue AS (\n    SELECT \n      o.store_id,\n      SUM(o.total_after_discount) AS total_revenue\n    FROM \n      orders o\n    WHERE \n      EXTRACT(QUARTER FROM o.created_date) = 4\n      AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM o.created_date) = 2025\n    GROUP BY \n      o.store_id\n  ),\n  \n  -- Number of canceled orders\n  canceled_orders AS (\n    SELECT \n      o.store_id,\n      COUNT(o.id) AS num_canceled_orders\n    FROM \n      orders o\n    WHERE \n      o.order_status = 'Đã hủy'\n    GROUP BY \n      o.store_id\n  ),\n  \n  -- Best-selling food item in history\n  best_selling_food AS (\n    SELECT \n      f.store_id,\n      f.title,\n      ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY f.store_id ORDER BY SUM(od.quantity) DESC) AS rn\n    FROM \n      order_detail od\n    JOIN \n      food f ON od.food_id = f.id\n    GROUP BY \n      f.store_id, f.title\n  ),\n  \n  -- Average rating of stores\n  store_ratings AS (\n    SELECT \n      f.store_id,\n      AVG(rf.point) AS avg_rating\n    FROM \n      rating_food rf\n    JOIN \n      orders o ON rf.order_id = o.id\n    JOIN \n      food f ON rf.food_id = f.id\n    GROUP BY \n      f.store_id\n  ),\n  \n  -- Stores with at least one promotional order\n  stores_with_promo AS (\n    SELECT DISTINCT \n      o.store_id\n    FROM \n      orders o\n    JOIN \n      order_promo op ON o.id = op.order_id\n  )\n\n-- Main query\nSELECT \n  s.id,\n  s.store_name,\n  COALESCE(sr.total_revenue, 0) AS total_revenue_q4_2025,\n  COALESCE(co.num_canceled_orders, 0) AS num_canceled_orders,\n  bsf.title AS best_selling_food,\n  COALESCE(sr.avg_rating, 0) AS avg_rating\nFROM \n  stores s\n  LEFT JOIN store_revenue sr ON s.id = sr.store_id\n  LEFT JOIN canceled_orders co ON s.id = co.store_id\n  LEFT JOIN best_selling_food bsf ON s.id = bsf.store_id AND bsf.rn = 1\n  LEFT JOIN store_ratings sr2 ON s.id = sr2.store_id\nWHERE \n  s.id IN (SELECT store_id FROM stores_with_promo);\n```\n\n### Explanation\n\nThe query uses several Common Table Expressions (CTEs) to calculate:\n\n1. `store_revenue`: Total revenue for each store in Q4 2025.\n2. `canceled_orders`: Number of canceled orders for each store.\n3. `best_selling_food`: Best-selling food item in history for each store.\n4. `store_ratings`: Average rating for each store.\n5. `stores_with_promo`: Stores with at least one promotional order.\n\nThe main query joins these CTEs with the `stores` table to retrieve the required information for each store that has had at least one promotional order. If a store does not have data in a particular CTE, the `LEFT JOIN` ensures that `NULL` values are replaced with `0` or an empty string as needed.	WITH \n  -- Revenue for Q4 2025\n  store_revenue AS (\n    SELECT \n      o.store_id,\n      SUM(o.total_after_discount) AS total_revenue\n    FROM \n      orders o\n    WHERE \n      EXTRACT(QUARTER FROM o.created_date) = 4\n      AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM o.created_date) = 2025\n    GROUP BY \n      o.store_id\n  ),\n  \n  -- Number of canceled orders\n  canceled_orders AS (\n    SELECT \n      o.store_id,\n      COUNT(o.id) AS num_canceled_orders\n    FROM \n      orders o\n    WHERE \n      o.order_status = 'Đã hủy'\n    GROUP BY \n      o.store_id\n  ),\n  \n  -- Best-selling food item in history\n  best_selling_food AS (\n    SELECT \n      f.store_id,\n      f.title,\n      ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY f.store_id ORDER BY SUM(od.quantity) DESC) AS rn\n    FROM \n      order_detail od\n    JOIN \n      food f ON od.food_id = f.id\n    GROUP BY \n      f.store_id, f.title\n  ),\n  \n  -- Average rating of stores\n  store_ratings AS (\n    SELECT \n      f.store_id,\n      AVG(rf.point) AS avg_rating\n    FROM \n      rating_food rf\n    JOIN \n      orders o ON rf.order_id = o.id\n    JOIN \n      food f ON rf.food_id = f.id\n    GROUP BY \n      f.store_id\n  ),\n  \n  -- Stores with at least one promotional order\n  stores_with_promo AS (\n    SELECT DISTINCT \n      o.store_id\n    FROM \n      orders o\n    JOIN \n      order_promo op ON o.id = op.order_id\n  )\n\n-- Main query\nSELECT \n  s.id,\n  s.store_name,\n  COALESCE(sr.total_revenue, 0) AS total_revenue_q4_2025,\n  COALESCE(co.num_canceled_orders, 0) AS num_canceled_orders,\n  bsf.title AS best_selling_food,\n  COALESCE(sr.avg_rating, 0) AS avg_rating\nFROM \n  stores s\n  LEFT JOIN store_revenue sr ON s.id = sr.store_id\n  LEFT JOIN canceled_orders co ON s.id = co.store_id\n  LEFT JOIN best_selling_food bsf ON s.id = bsf.store_id AND bsf.rn = 1\n  LEFT JOIN store_ratings sr2 ON s.id = sr2.store_id\nWHERE \n  s.id IN (SELECT store_id FROM stores_with_promo);	2026-06-19 08:25:34.20955+07	chat	null
