.dept_no\nLEFT JOIN Dept_Salaries ds ON d.dept_no = ds.dept_no\nGROUP BY d.dept_no, d.dept_name;\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1.  **Q1_Employees (CTE):** Filters employees whose tenure overlaps with the Q1 2000 window.\n2.  **Active_Employees_End_Q1 (CTE):** Filters employees whose tenure includes the specific date `2000-06-30`.\n3.  **Dept_Salaries (CTE):** Calculates the sum of salaries for employees active on the final day of the quarter.\n4.  **Title_Counts (CTE):** Aggregates the count of each job title per department for active employees.\n5.  **Main Query:**\n    *   Joins the CTEs with the `departments` table.\n    *   Calculates the `turnover_rate` using the provided formula and `ROUND` function.\n    *   Uses a correlated subquery to extract the `most_frequent_title` by ordering the `Title_Counts` by frequency and selecting the top result.\n    *   Uses `COALESCE` to handle departments that might not have salary data recorded for that specific date.	WITH Q1_Employees AS (\n    -- Employees present at any point during Q1 2000\n    SELECT dept_no, emp_no\n    FROM dept_emp\n    WHERE from_date <= '2000-06-30' AND to_date >= '2000-04-01'\n),\nActive_Employees_End_Q1 AS (\n    -- Employees active on the last day of Q1 2000\n    SELECT dept_no, emp_no\n    FROM dept_emp\n    WHERE '2000-06-30' BETWEEN from_date AND to_date\n),\nDept_Salaries AS (\n    -- Salary of active employees at the end of Q1 2000\n    SELECT ae.dept_no, SUM(s.salary) as total_salary\n    FROM Active_Employees_End_Q1 ae\n    JOIN salaries s ON ae.emp_no = s.emp_no\n    WHERE '2000-06-30' BETWEEN s.from_date AND s.to_date\n    GROUP BY ae.dept_no\n),\nTitle_Counts AS (\n    -- Count titles for active employees to find the most frequent one\n    SELECT ae.dept_no, t.title, COUNT(*) as title_count\n    FROM Active_Employees_End_Q1 ae\n    JOIN titles t ON ae.emp_no = t.emp_no\n    WHERE '2000-06-30' BETWEEN t.from_date AND t.to_date\n    GROUP BY ae.dept_no, t.title\n)\nSELECT \n    d.dept_no, \